            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0929" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/552: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grummon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-04T16:00:00+03:00">July 4, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 4—11:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>363. Department’s 73, June 27, 4 p.m. I discussed the renewal of the commercial
                    agreement with Potemkin yesterday who said that he would consult with the
                    Commissariat for Foreign Trade and inform the Embassy promptly of the Soviet
                    Government’s point of view. He stated that Umansky had discussed the matter with
                    the Secretary and he thought also with the President prior to his departure on
                    leave. He expressed himself as in agreement as to the desirability of dealing
                    with the matter promptly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grummon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
